Subject: Make light frames visible to the debugger entry points

What this does
  Make light frames visible to the debugger entry points.

Why we need it
  `js_get_stack_frame_at_level`, `JS_GetStackDepth`, `JS_GetLocalVariablesAtLevel`, `JS_SetVariableAtLevel`, `JS_GetFrameInfoAtLevel` and `JS_EvalInStackFrame` walked `current_stack_frame -> prev_frame` only; a light frame has no `JSStackFrame`, so the debugger saw a short stack, no name/line for light frames, and could not read their arguments or locals.

What it adds
  One logical-stack iterator (`regvm_debug_iter_*`, shared with `regvm_fill_backtrace_frames`) yields light and real frames innermost-first; a light frame is materialized into caller-provided scratch storage; `JS_GetFrameInfoAtLevel` resolves a register pc through the callee's `ret_ip`/the captured ip; eval on a light frame gets a full-width read-only variable-area copy and publishes the frame's registers as roots for the call; a promoted slot (>= `regvm_var_count`) reads as `undefined`, never out of bounds, and `JS_SetVariableAtLevel` refuses it (a record frame writes an unread slot).

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
